# Optional Azure Speech Question Transcription

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: Optional after local baseline; not an answer prerequisite
Dependencies: 27_AI_ANSWER_RESEARCH.todo, 33_ANSWER_LATENCY_QUALITY.todo

## Purpose

Evaluate cloud ASR only if local question quality/latency fails a measured requirement and raw-audio processing is approved.

## Tasks

- [ ] Obtain separate cloud-audio policy/profile and selected-source/region/budget approval.
- [ ] Compare continuous Azure Speech on identical synthetic PCM; Fast/file and Batch are not live substitutes.
- [ ] Validate phrase hints, segmentation/stability properties and real measured latency.
- [ ] If explicit commit is needed, verify Speech SDK1.52+ preview support/format/region and CommitToken behavior.
- [ ] Preserve source isolation, manual Ask, no automatic responses and visible cloud-audio status.
- [ ] Keep Azure Realtime audio/VAD as a separately evaluated alternative, not required infrastructure.
- [ ] Promote only after evidence; never auto-fallback from local ASR to cloud audio.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Any cloud audio is deliberate, scoped and accurately disclosed.
- [ ] It improves a defined quality/latency target without unapproved privacy or preview dependencies.
- [ ] Local ASR plus Azure text answers still works independently.

## Completion evidence

- None. No Azure Speech request or cloud-audio configuration was performed.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-08 - Explicitly optional; local transcription remains the recommended baseline.
